WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.344 --> 00:00:06.724
Milan.

00:00:07.184 --> 00:00:16.711
On the 19th of October last year, 3,000 people came to pay their final respects to Lea, brutally killed by the Calabrian mafia, the&nbsp;'Ndrangheta.

00:00:22.102 --> 00:00:22.359
Lea,

00:00:23.797 --> 00:00:27.483
you listened to your conscience and you broke the mafia's code of silence.

00:00:31.172 --> 00:00:35.959
The most beautiful way to describe you today is to say that you were a witness to truth.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:39.748
Ciao, Lea.

00:00:42.326 --> 00:00:44.374
Lea&nbsp;Garofalo was 35.

00:00:45.107 --> 00:00:48.257
She had denounced members of her own family to investigators.

00:00:48.698 --> 00:00:52.131
She wanted to give her daughter a better future away from clan violence.

00:00:53.403 --> 00:00:58.851
Anti-mafia organisations and representatives of the state have come to praise the courage of this woman.

00:01:01.939 --> 00:01:05.701
Which her lawyer reminds us of in reading this letter, which Lea wrote.

00:01:06.546 --> 00:01:09.225
A cry for help sent to the President of the Republic.

00:01:10.328 --> 00:01:13.328
The worst thing is that I already know the destiny that awaits me.

00:01:14.875 --> 00:01:17.483
Having lost everything, I will die.

00:01:20.694 --> 00:01:24.725
With this letter, I would like to change the course of my sad story.

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:27.242
I need help.

00:01:27.725 --> 00:01:28.600
Someone help me.

00:01:29.304 --> 00:01:31.210
I'm a young mother who is desperate.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:33.056
Ciao, Lea.

00:01:36.903 --> 00:01:39.305
Denise, her 22-year-old daughter, is here.

00:01:41.052 --> 00:01:44.282
For her own safety, she has to remain hidden behind this window.

00:01:49.162 --> 00:01:50.101
Hello, everyone.

00:01:51.584 --> 00:01:53.685
I thank you with all my heart for coming.

00:02:00.974 --> 00:02:01.224
This...

00:02:04.632 --> 00:02:07.673
is a very difficult day for me.

00:02:10.482 --> 00:02:14.217
But I have found the strength to pick myself up.

00:02:16.084 --> 00:02:16.403
Mama,

00:02:17.622 --> 00:02:18.764
if all this has happened,

00:02:19.365 --> 00:02:20.637
it's for my benefit,

00:02:21.915 --> 00:02:23.809
and I will always be grateful to you.

00:02:25.169 --> 00:02:25.919
Goodbye, Mama.

00:02:29.403 --> 00:02:32.376
For the Calabrian mafia, silence is the rule.

00:02:33.216 --> 00:02:36.112
Those who speak out, the traitors, are eliminated.

00:02:37.058 --> 00:02:41.298
Today, wives of mafia families have decided to stand up against the&nbsp;'Ndrangheta.

00:02:41.623 --> 00:02:47.108
Putting their lives in danger, they have said no to one of the most powerful mafia organizations in the world.

00:02:54.401 --> 00:02:57.168
MAFIA: THE BETRAYAL OF WOMEN

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:27.431
In the south of Italy, facing Sicily, is Calabria.

00:03:28.923 --> 00:03:32.450
A poor region not much bigger than 12,000 square kilometres.

00:03:33.731 --> 00:03:38.879
It is populated by farmers and shepherds, which is traditionally a region of emigration.

00:03:41.591 --> 00:03:44.259
Calabria is also home to the&nbsp;'Ndrangheta.

00:03:44.973 --> 00:03:49.981
A formidable criminal organisation which controls every square centimetre of the territory.

00:03:55.768 --> 00:04:01.538
The Calabrian mafia draws its strength from the heart of the Aspromonte Mountains, where access is difficult.

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:10.499
Long-time specialists in kidnapping, they would hide their hostages in the dense forest.

00:04:16.098 --> 00:04:19.067
Forests, which also shelter the site of a cult.

00:04:21.567 --> 00:04:23.773
The sanctuary of Our Lady of Polsi.

00:04:29.992 --> 00:04:38.013
Every year, on the 2nd of September, thousands of Calabrians make the pilgrimage here to praise the Virgin Mary and ask for her protection.

00:04:47.036 --> 00:04:53.240
48 hours of uninterrupted fervour and traditional songs and dances to the rhythm of tambourines.

00:05:00.887 --> 00:05:03.989
A gathering which the&nbsp;'Ndrangheta&nbsp;managed to appropriate.

00:05:05.211 --> 00:05:08.694
A fact condemned by the bishop of Polsi in a surprising speech.

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:19.406
Historic events over the last century have linked this sanctuary to the sad phenomenon of organized crime.

00:05:23.343 --> 00:05:30.108
Unfortunately, and in blasphemous fashion, Our Lady of Polsi is seen as the Madonna of the&nbsp;'Ndrangheta.

00:05:33.648 --> 00:05:36.990
The shadow of the Calabrian mafia looms over the whole assembly.

00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:43.310
Mingling with the faithful are mafiosos, who have come from all 4 corners of the planet.

00:05:44.387 --> 00:05:52.078
The&nbsp;'Ndrangheta, an organization whose members today are spread across the entire world, meet here, every year, by the Madonna.

00:05:55.574 --> 00:05:57.655
The bishop is addressing them directly.

00:05:59.483 --> 00:06:05.889
I am bold enough to make a final plea to those amongst you who are still able to change.

00:06:08.574 --> 00:06:11.714
To finally put an end to and stop this corruption.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:20.512
The production and trafficking of drugs, bribery, homicide, gambling,

00:06:21.824 --> 00:06:24.230
living off others. We know it's a facade.

00:06:26.307 --> 00:06:27.651
So, in the name of God.

00:06:28.584 --> 00:06:29.723
And of the Virgin Mary,

00:06:30.463 --> 00:06:32.404
which you proclaim so fervently.

00:06:33.264 --> 00:06:34.146
In their names,

00:06:34.646 --> 00:06:36.584
I ask you to put down your arms,

00:06:37.507 --> 00:06:38.108
hand them in,

00:06:39.264 --> 00:06:39.966
destroy them.

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:45.927
These prayers are in vain.

00:06:47.444 --> 00:06:54.271
In reality, the pilgrimage is often the occasion which allows the mafia to meet in order to make important decisions.

00:06:55.271 --> 00:06:57.427
The&nbsp;'Ndrangheta&nbsp;is a feudal society.

00:06:57.887 --> 00:06:59.769
Where the rule of silence reigns.

00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:08.218
A rule of silence which even Don Pino Strangio, the priest in charge of the sanctuary, does not break.

00:07:12.663 --> 00:07:14.663
There are no mafia meetings in Polsi.

00:07:15.146 --> 00:07:18.771
People just meet here to exchange ideas and their thoughts on life.

00:07:21.271 --> 00:07:25.319
Of course, they sometimes make decisions and choose to do wrong.

00:07:28.843 --> 00:07:30.463
But I think that the true believer,

00:07:31.105 --> 00:07:33.084
the pilgrim who comes here to Polsi,

00:07:33.627 --> 00:07:34.783
is quite different.

00:07:39.550 --> 00:07:47.002
The&nbsp;'Ndrangheta, an invisible 100-year-old group, has become one of the most powerful criminal organizations in the world.

00:07:53.769 --> 00:07:58.350
A few kilometers from here a member of the Calabrian mafia has agreed to meet us.

00:08:02.844 --> 00:08:05.305
Mastro Ciccio, age 73.

00:08:06.983 --> 00:08:12.329
Officially, he was a baker. but at the age of 17, he entered the service of his clan.

00:08:14.031 --> 00:08:16.235
When I first started, this is how it happened.

00:08:17.781 --> 00:08:20.439
They made a cut in my left hand, and the bosses.

00:08:21.163 --> 00:08:26.846
We were united with our blood, swearing never to betray our honorable society, our clan.

00:08:28.045 --> 00:08:30.139
You always have to obey the boss's orders.

00:08:31.350 --> 00:08:32.942
He was the one who baptized me.

00:08:33.865 --> 00:08:35.130
He's the only one in command.

00:08:35.966 --> 00:08:36.606
The only one.

00:08:39.567 --> 00:08:47.711
The head of the clan finishes the baptismal ceremony by burning a tiny image of Saint Michael the Archangel, the patron saint of the 'Ndrangheta.

00:08:48.192 --> 00:08:49.331
The threat is clear.

00:08:49.677 --> 00:08:53.274
If you betray us, you will burn in the same way as this holy image.

00:08:55.596 --> 00:08:59.862
Mastro Ciccio wants to show his tattoos, a code of honor on the skin.

00:09:06.408 --> 00:09:07.985
This is the Rose of the Winds.

00:09:09.048 --> 00:09:12.610
It signifies that the&nbsp;'Ndrangheta&nbsp;is present all over the world.

00:09:14.908 --> 00:09:18.543
The&nbsp;'Ndrangheta&nbsp;is a seed that we sow in all winds.

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:21.658
All over the whole world, there are accomplices,

00:09:22.957 --> 00:09:23.860
representatives.

00:09:25.302 --> 00:09:27.942
The butterfly means that you must remain humble,

00:09:29.606 --> 00:09:30.403
like a butterfly.

00:09:31.629 --> 00:09:33.388
Not shy, but never arrogant.

00:09:35.251 --> 00:09:38.775
There, it says, "As long as I live, I shall not fall in the mud."

00:09:41.857 --> 00:09:43.421
That means I will never dishonour.

00:09:44.857 --> 00:09:46.264
It means that I'll never betray.

00:09:48.506 --> 00:09:49.068
Traitors.

00:09:50.006 --> 00:09:51.867
The&nbsp;'Ndrangheta&nbsp;hardly has any.

00:09:53.085 --> 00:09:55.475
This sprawling mafia is based on blood ties.

00:09:57.115 --> 00:10:00.131
Family units, closely knit, called cosca.

00:10:02.177 --> 00:10:07.738
At the heart of the family, rules are strict: the men do the business, the women have no rights.

00:10:10.294 --> 00:10:12.400
A woman must do the household chores.

00:10:13.475 --> 00:10:15.285
She cannot take part in our affairs.

00:10:16.856 --> 00:10:17.623
She must be a woman.

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:18.778
No more.

00:10:26.192 --> 00:10:28.960
Unexpectedly, one of them has agreed to meet us.

00:10:30.895 --> 00:10:35.783
Hiding behind her scarf, she tells of an everyday life of stashes and drugs.

00:10:36.169 --> 00:10:40.125
My sisters and I understood it all from the age of 10 or 11.

00:10:41.131 --> 00:10:43.818
We saw the raids, the trafficking in the house.

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:47.828
Then you begin to realise what kind of world you live in.

00:10:51.038 --> 00:10:53.713
You ask your mother, and she explains everything.

00:10:55.273 --> 00:10:58.398
Everything you see and hear has to stay buried inside you.

00:10:59.455 --> 00:11:04.955
I know the places where my father hides things, but I would never tell, even if I was tortured to death.

00:11:06.721 --> 00:11:09.016
We have to hide the weapons, the ammunition.

00:11:09.488 --> 00:11:13.799
We know about the drugs, all the trafficking, but we can't say anything.

00:11:17.432 --> 00:11:22.152
When my father murders someone, I know when he did it and how he did it.

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:28.043
And in your opinion, are all the women in all the clans aware?

00:11:30.599 --> 00:11:31.729
Yes, nearly all.

00:11:33.822 --> 00:11:40.208
Daughter of a boss, at 22, she has always respected clan law, which guarantees her protection and wealth.

00:11:41.345 --> 00:11:42.641
Everyone respects us.

00:11:42.854 --> 00:11:44.186
We never go out alone.

00:11:44.794 --> 00:11:47.465
We're always the junior members of the clan.

00:11:48.817 --> 00:11:54.615
If a young man approaches without asking my father's permission, or from the junior members chaperoning us,

00:11:55.740 --> 00:11:58.020
he will be hit, or get threatened.

00:12:01.054 --> 00:12:03.548
You can also go into the shops without paying.

00:12:04.379 --> 00:12:06.398
You never have to wait to see a doctor.

00:12:07.059 --> 00:12:11.286
As soon as he knows who you are, you are seen before everyone else.

00:12:12.063 --> 00:12:13.213
People respect you.

00:12:13.587 --> 00:12:16.242
You go into a bar, and it's all free.

00:12:17.048 --> 00:12:22.251
In this life, luxuries and money come easily. You get respect. Every door is open for you.

00:12:25.705 --> 00:12:28.017
A mafia lifestyle with its codes of honour.

00:12:29.174 --> 00:12:30.677
A life which Lea betrayed.

00:12:31.876 --> 00:12:33.317
Her punishment was death.

00:12:39.888 --> 00:12:45.365
Lea was born in Petilia Policastro, a village with a population of 9,000.

00:12:48.395 --> 00:12:53.365
She belonged to one of the most powerful mafia families in the region, the Garofalo.

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:57.071
Lea's brother, Floriano, was the local boss.

00:13:00.105 --> 00:13:07.830
Ever since she was 15 years old, she had only one desire, to flee the village of her birth and her destiny as a daughter of the mafia.

00:13:07.937 --> 00:13:11.495
Her lawyer, Vincenza Rando, became her confidante before she died.

00:13:12.299 --> 00:13:15.426
She told me, "My father was killed when I was a baby.

00:13:15.941 --> 00:13:18.043
My grandfather and my uncle were killed."

00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:22.168
I had this image of women and family always dressed in black.

00:13:22.855 --> 00:13:24.635
We were always in mourning.

00:13:26.698 --> 00:13:32.048
At 15, Lea already knew that the&nbsp;'Ndrangheta brought nothing but death.

00:13:33.890 --> 00:13:36.812
In the summer, when she is 15, Lea falls in love.

00:13:38.097 --> 00:13:45.019
She runs away to Milan with her new boyfriend, Carlo Cosco, in the hope of finding a new life, far away from the mafia.

00:13:47.989 --> 00:13:50.629
Lea and Carlo move into this building near the station.

00:13:52.394 --> 00:13:57.886
She doesn't know that it is the headquarters of the Cosco clan, and a hot spot for dealing in Milan.

00:13:59.288 --> 00:14:04.711
The clan had absolute control over the building, where it carried out all its illegal business. They dealt drugs,

00:14:06.535 --> 00:14:08.947
they stashed cocaine, which they sold on,

00:14:09.817 --> 00:14:12.403
they controlled the whole neighbourhood of the Via Montello.

00:14:13.325 --> 00:14:16.543
In this sector, everyone knew who the Cosco were.

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:23.445
Lea realized that Carlo had wooed her for a very specific reason.

00:14:25.154 --> 00:14:33.065
Carlo hadn't chosen her because he was in love, but because she was the sister of Floriano&nbsp;Garofalo, a&nbsp;'Ndrangheta&nbsp;boss.

00:14:33.542 --> 00:14:36.667
And Carlo wanted a career in the&nbsp;'Ndrangheta.

00:14:38.447 --> 00:14:42.729
Powerless, Lea is forced to continue to live the life she wanted to escape.

00:14:43.509 --> 00:14:47.182
She sees everything, hears everything, but she has to keep silent.

00:14:48.352 --> 00:14:52.147
At 17, she becomes a mother, and her life becomes a living hell.

00:14:53.736 --> 00:14:56.859
He didn't let her go out. He didn't give her any money.

00:14:57.197 --> 00:15:05.408
One day, she stood up to him and said, "If you don't change your life, I'm leaving. I don't want to bring up my daughter like this."

00:15:07.783 --> 00:15:08.894
Carlo abuses her.

00:15:09.658 --> 00:15:11.378
He becomes increasingly violent.

00:15:12.158 --> 00:15:13.674
It lasts for 11 years.

00:15:17.421 --> 00:15:21.962
Finally, in 2002, in order to escape, Lea does the unthinkable.

00:15:23.320 --> 00:15:27.276
She places herself under police protection and tells them everything.

00:15:27.418 --> 00:15:30.489
The trafficking, the stashes, the names of the bosses.

00:15:30.871 --> 00:15:32.243
But the police do nothing.

00:15:32.595 --> 00:15:35.013
No one at the center of the Cosco clan is worried.

00:15:35.417 --> 00:15:36.640
Lea is desperate.

00:15:38.028 --> 00:15:42.278
For unexplained reasons, difficulty with the inquiry, lack of proof,

00:15:43.278 --> 00:15:44.888
her declarations were useless.

00:15:48.729 --> 00:15:51.271
For 7 years, the inquiry drags on.

00:15:53.276 --> 00:15:55.101
Lea's life gets no better.

00:15:55.603 --> 00:15:59.113
Shunted from hotel to hotel by the police charged with protecting her.

00:16:01.504 --> 00:16:02.606
Justice failed.

00:16:03.763 --> 00:16:10.138
Here is someone who turned to the state, and the answer she got forced her back into the arms of her aggressor.

00:16:12.918 --> 00:16:20.275
7 years after betraying her clan, at the end of her tether Lea calls her ex-partner Carlo to ask him for help.

00:16:22.837 --> 00:16:24.318
He offers to see her in Milan.

00:16:25.041 --> 00:16:25.822
But it's a trap.

00:16:27.298 --> 00:16:32.696
Vincenza Rando, her lawyer, does everything in her power to dissuade her from going, in vain.

00:16:33.853 --> 00:16:35.626
It's as if she had a meeting with destiny.

00:16:36.033 --> 00:16:43.208
She said to me, "Mom, may God bless you. I thank you very much for what you are doing, but now I have to go to Milan.

00:16:43.321 --> 00:16:48.255
And you see, nothing will happen to me. I promise you, I will be very careful."

00:16:49.692 --> 00:16:54.707
For this meeting, Lea's life insurance is Denise, the daughter she had with Carlo.

00:16:58.359 --> 00:17:01.919
CCTV cameras film the two young women in the streets of Milan.

00:17:02.429 --> 00:17:06.288
Denise, 17 at the time, dressed in black, and Lea in white.

00:17:07.413 --> 00:17:08.646
They are going to meet Carlo.

00:17:10.244 --> 00:17:12.851
It's the 24th of November, 2009.

00:17:18.669 --> 00:17:22.369
Carlo leaves with Denise, leaving Lea alone on the pavement.

00:17:23.671 --> 00:17:25.481
These are the last images of Lea.

00:17:28.409 --> 00:17:30.009
Denise can't get hold of her mother.

00:17:30.471 --> 00:17:32.264
In a panic, she calls Lea's sister.

00:17:35.916 --> 00:17:39.445
I told Denise immediately, they have made your mother disappear.

00:17:40.057 --> 00:17:43.568
She started crying, saying, "It's not true, I don't believe it.

00:17:44.151 --> 00:17:45.288
She was with my father."

00:17:45.807 --> 00:17:48.057
I replied that he was the one who did it.

00:17:48.376 --> 00:17:49.597
There was no doubt in your mind?

00:17:49.737 --> 00:17:51.198
No, I never had any doubt.

00:17:52.939 --> 00:17:54.965
The court never had any doubt, either.

00:17:55.765 --> 00:18:02.439
In 2012, Carlo and five members of the clan are sentenced to 25 years in prison for Lea's murder.

00:18:06.773 --> 00:18:08.980
One year later, an appeal begins.

00:18:12.336 --> 00:18:15.009
At the Court of Justice in Milan, the crowds are gathered.

00:18:16.195 --> 00:18:18.829
Behind the bars, Carlo and his accomplices.

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:27.162
Carlo wants to make a confession to the court.

00:18:28.808 --> 00:18:34.575
A dramatic coup, having always denied murdering his partner for the first time, he's going to admit it.

00:18:40.307 --> 00:18:43.186
I confess to the homicide of Lea Garofalo.

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:53.935
I want to say that I do not understand why today my daughter Denise is under state protection.

00:18:58.383 --> 00:18:59.923
Who should she be protected from?

00:19:01.938 --> 00:19:03.779
I would give my life for my daughter.

00:19:04.880 --> 00:19:07.204
I deserve her hatred because I killed her mother.

00:19:07.961 --> 00:19:10.134
Woe betide anyone who touches my daughter.

00:19:10.650 --> 00:19:12.453
I pray that one day she will forgive me.

00:19:13.377 --> 00:19:13.883
Thank you.

00:19:19.939 --> 00:19:23.983
A few days later, it's the turn of his daughter, Denise, to give evidence.

00:19:27.236 --> 00:19:34.169
Positioned behind the screen so that no one can recognize her, she tells of the days following her mother, Lea's disappearance.

00:19:35.890 --> 00:19:40.413
Alone and confused, Denise is afraid of her father, and refuses to see him.

00:19:42.779 --> 00:19:47.921
A few days after my mother disappeared, it was my 18th birthday.

00:19:50.108 --> 00:19:54.186
My father insisted on organizing a birthday party for me.

00:19:55.890 --> 00:19:59.246
He called my friends, and lots of other people.

00:20:00.438 --> 00:20:02.935
But they celebrated without me.

00:20:08.590 --> 00:20:10.904
I refused to go to the party.

00:20:13.693 --> 00:20:18.029
After Denise's evidence, behind the screen, tongues are loosened.

00:20:20.201 --> 00:20:25.287
A member of the clan has also decided to collaborate with the law in exchange for early release.

00:20:26.342 --> 00:20:30.041
Carmine Venturino was charged with having disposed of Lea's body.

00:20:32.086 --> 00:20:33.543
We went up to the apartment,

00:20:34.743 --> 00:20:40.375
and as soon as we put on the light, we saw Lea Garofalo's body, which was on the floor.

00:20:42.232 --> 00:20:43.099
We turned her over.

00:20:44.381 --> 00:20:46.544
She had marks of blows on her face

00:20:47.723 --> 00:20:50.562
And her clothes were ripped around her chest.

00:20:53.490 --> 00:20:57.817
There was a green lace around her neck, which she had been strangled with.

00:20:58.756 --> 00:21:01.138
We took the body, and put it in a box.

00:21:04.258 --> 00:21:10.180
Carmine Venturino and an accomplice took the box with Lea's body about 15 kilometers out of Milan.

00:21:12.024 --> 00:21:13.251
Behind this fence.

00:21:15.579 --> 00:21:23.573
Once we were there, we got a barrel, and then we put Lea's body into it, head down, and set fire to it with petrol.

00:21:25.516 --> 00:21:28.963
After his confession, fragments of Lea's body were found.

00:21:31.729 --> 00:21:36.109
The inquiry found that after being burnt, her body was dissolved in acid.

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:42.489
The appeal court upheld the convictions for 5 of the 6 found guilty.

00:21:45.144 --> 00:21:53.794
In the name of the Italian people, the second section of the Milan Court of Appeal upholds the sentence of 25 years' imprisonment for the accused.

00:21:54.340 --> 00:22:00.903
Carlo Cosco, Giuseppe Cosco, Vito Cosco, Rosario Curcio, Massimo Sabatino.

00:22:08.990 --> 00:22:15.688
In Petilia Policastro, in the little village where Lea was born, her sister Marisa takes us to the cemetery.

00:22:17.041 --> 00:22:21.940
She shows us how all her family has fallen victim to the unrelenting laws of the&nbsp;'Ndrangheta.

00:22:23.823 --> 00:22:24.979
Here's my mother's tomb.

00:22:25.979 --> 00:22:27.182
And also my father's.

00:22:30.073 --> 00:22:30.916
This is my brother.

00:22:31.807 --> 00:22:34.131
Sadly, all my family is here.

00:22:35.773 --> 00:22:36.818
I'm the last one.

00:22:37.718 --> 00:22:39.359
They were killed by the 'Ndrangheta?

00:22:40.203 --> 00:22:44.366
Yes, my brother, my father, my sister, all of them.

00:22:45.446 --> 00:22:48.323
My brother was killed because he was supposed to punish Lea.

00:22:49.590 --> 00:22:52.619
He was supposed to get rid of my sister, but he didn't.

00:22:57.450 --> 00:23:03.325
He would never have been able to kill her, so he killed himself before Lea was eliminated.

00:23:06.597 --> 00:23:09.506
Lea was not only eliminated by the&nbsp;'Ndrangheta.

00:23:10.403 --> 00:23:13.985
Her story also appears to have been erased from the whole village's memory.

00:23:19.289 --> 00:23:21.523
I wanted to know what you think of this story.

00:23:22.361 --> 00:23:26.156
I don't know. I've never lived here. I've always lived abroad.

00:23:27.813 --> 00:23:29.518
I've been away for 60 years.

00:23:29.906 --> 00:23:32.406
60 years? So no one has an opinion on this story?

00:23:33.420 --> 00:23:34.047
What story?

00:23:35.720 --> 00:23:37.690
You don't know the story of Lea Garofalo?

00:23:37.811 --> 00:23:39.044
No. Oh, yes.

00:23:40.963 --> 00:23:41.968
Well, no, I don't.

00:23:43.607 --> 00:23:45.613
Do you know what happened with Lea Garofalo?

00:23:49.390 --> 00:23:50.151
No, I don't.

00:23:50.511 --> 00:23:51.662
Don't you know the story?

00:23:52.041 --> 00:23:53.713
No, no, no. I don't know what you're talking about.

00:23:55.119 --> 00:23:58.014
I was never here. I was in hospital. Absent.

00:23:59.651 --> 00:24:02.719
So, none of you have an opinion. And I'm sitting at the village bar.

00:24:08.660 --> 00:24:09.645
Okay, thank you.

00:24:12.922 --> 00:24:14.886
The rule of silence once more.

00:24:16.663 --> 00:24:18.255
We try our luck at the church.

00:24:18.968 --> 00:24:21.515
With the priest who conducted the mass in memory of Lea.

00:24:22.890 --> 00:24:25.358
We question him and pretend that we are not filming.

00:24:27.672 --> 00:24:27.936
Hello.

00:24:29.280 --> 00:24:30.515
I'm a friend of Lea's.

00:24:31.905 --> 00:24:34.180
Would you be prepared to talk to me about it?

00:24:36.933 --> 00:24:39.108
No, I arrived a lot later.

00:24:39.597 --> 00:24:40.554
I never knew her.

00:24:40.797 --> 00:24:41.839
Just a few minutes.

00:24:42.258 --> 00:24:43.519
I'm telling you, I didn't know her.

00:24:43.980 --> 00:24:45.651
Are you scared to talk about it?

00:24:45.824 --> 00:24:49.286
No, no, I don't know anything. Nothing at all. Nothing at all.

00:24:49.683 --> 00:24:50.488
Are you filming?

00:24:50.567 --> 00:24:53.447
No, we're not filming. I'd like to ask you some questions.

00:24:53.653 --> 00:24:58.261
And I've told you, I can't talk about something that I don't know about.

00:24:58.511 --> 00:24:59.763
But you have an opinion?

00:25:00.339 --> 00:25:01.996
No, I don't know anything.

00:25:02.605 --> 00:25:04.171
I can't invent what I don't know.

00:25:06.256 --> 00:25:07.415
I don't know anything.

00:25:08.317 --> 00:25:08.655
Okay.

00:25:09.758 --> 00:25:10.219
Goodbye.

00:25:10.726 --> 00:25:12.016
Nobody knows anything.

00:25:13.714 --> 00:25:16.261
But Lea's family has not completely disappeared.

00:25:17.500 --> 00:25:19.734
This man in the striped t-shirt is her uncle.

00:25:20.444 --> 00:25:23.800
He remembers, particularly, that Carlo, her killer, was a charming man.

00:25:24.894 --> 00:25:28.288
With me, Carlo Cosco always behaved very well.

00:25:29.738 --> 00:25:30.623
He admired me.

00:25:32.847 --> 00:25:34.263
Came to eat at my house.

00:25:35.537 --> 00:25:38.343
Lea was a nice girl. I cannot judge either of them.

00:25:39.240 --> 00:25:40.451
Yeah, but he killed her.

00:25:40.842 --> 00:25:41.604
That I don't know.

00:25:52.568 --> 00:25:54.128
After what happened to my sister,

00:25:55.709 --> 00:25:56.845
people are afraid.

00:25:57.584 --> 00:25:59.073
They're frightened of speaking,

00:25:59.459 --> 00:26:00.867
of putting themselves at risk,

00:26:01.349 --> 00:26:02.596
of appearing on television.

00:26:05.992 --> 00:26:08.860
The&nbsp;'Ndrangheta&nbsp;have threatened to kill my son

00:26:09.764 --> 00:26:12.367
because I spoke about Lea on television.

00:26:13.759 --> 00:26:14.979
They can do anything.

00:26:16.721 --> 00:26:18.659
They start with threats,

00:26:19.065 --> 00:26:20.392
they torch your car,

00:26:21.080 --> 00:26:22.559
set fire to your house.

00:26:24.237 --> 00:26:26.024
Their warnings are very precise.

00:26:27.159 --> 00:26:30.159
If you ignore them, they will definitely kill you.

00:26:37.115 --> 00:26:38.915
Marisa takes us to Caterina's.

00:26:40.150 --> 00:26:44.316
She's the only one of Lea's friends in the village who dares to talk about what happened.

00:26:49.160 --> 00:26:52.344
Amongst ourselves, we say that Lea did the right thing,

00:26:53.121 --> 00:26:56.886
but no one can publicly stand up to her ex-husband.

00:27:01.418 --> 00:27:03.568
Why is he dangerous? Is he powerful?

00:27:04.877 --> 00:27:05.708
I think

00:27:07.053 --> 00:27:08.404
that the mafia,

00:27:09.058 --> 00:27:13.063
are people who belong to this family are powerful.

00:27:14.727 --> 00:27:16.651
We grew up in this culture.

00:27:17.866 --> 00:27:20.657
People who live by illegal means,

00:27:20.989 --> 00:27:23.281
that have power, and so,

00:27:24.110 --> 00:27:26.210
no one wants to stand up to them.

00:27:27.805 --> 00:27:28.680
The Coscos.

00:27:29.524 --> 00:27:31.383
No one can touch them in the region.

00:27:33.352 --> 00:27:36.539
We met one of the very few reformed bosses of the&nbsp;'Ndrangheta.

00:27:39.018 --> 00:27:42.643
He agreed to meet us at his home, where he lives under state protection.

00:27:44.346 --> 00:27:48.166
Luigi Bonaventura was head of a clan which worked with the Cosco.

00:27:49.938 --> 00:27:57.096
Sentenced to 15 years in prison for two murders, he was involved in activities from trafficking drugs to extortion.

00:27:58.393 --> 00:28:02.579
Like all the men in the&nbsp;'Ndrangheta, Luigi was brought up like a child soldier.

00:28:02.912 --> 00:28:04.744
Programmed to take over from his father.

00:28:06.457 --> 00:28:09.038
I remember shooting for the first time when I was 10.

00:28:09.859 --> 00:28:11.359
I don't know if I did before.

00:28:12.538 --> 00:28:17.063
Then, from 12 to 14, I had specific training in different types of weapons.

00:28:20.633 --> 00:28:22.570
From Kalashnikovs to rifles,

00:28:23.836 --> 00:28:25.784
from pistols to machine guns,

00:28:26.352 --> 00:28:27.883
and so on, and so on.

00:28:29.836 --> 00:28:31.102
They taught us to kill people.

00:28:32.540 --> 00:28:35.804
Yes, they teach us to kill from a very early age.

00:28:38.726 --> 00:28:41.746
His mother tried to fight against this education as best she could.

00:28:43.691 --> 00:28:44.394
My poor mother.

00:28:46.777 --> 00:28:50.459
She was beaten, kicked, pistol whipped, standing up to my father.

00:28:51.432 --> 00:28:53.127
She didn't want me brought up like that.

00:28:56.917 --> 00:29:01.435
Luigi understands women who, like Lea, rebel at the heart of the&nbsp;'Ndrangheta.

00:29:02.996 --> 00:29:05.477
He has followed the trial of the young woman's assassins.

00:29:06.257 --> 00:29:10.844
According to him, at his hearing, Carlo did far more than read out a letter.

00:29:11.315 --> 00:29:13.521
He sent a message to the Calabrian mafia.

00:29:21.159 --> 00:29:23.424
First, he touches his ear, which means listen.

00:29:29.523 --> 00:29:31.665
Then he touches his eye to say, look.

00:29:38.836 --> 00:29:42.258
Then he touches his mouth to make them understand he will say nothing.

00:29:46.155 --> 00:29:51.484
He gave other clear messages, like the jacket he had over his shoulders while he was talking.

00:29:54.655 --> 00:29:59.499
The jacket means that Carlo Cosco has moved up the ranks, that he deserves respect.

00:30:03.088 --> 00:30:05.230
He wanted to reassure the&nbsp;'Ndrangheta.

00:30:06.832 --> 00:30:07.652
He won't talk.

00:30:09.457 --> 00:30:12.852
He will assume all responsibility, but in exchange,

00:30:13.957 --> 00:30:17.769
he makes it clear that no-one should touch his daughter Denise.

00:30:22.742 --> 00:30:27.092
He is paying the price for what he did, and to guarantee his daughter's immunity.

00:30:27.443 --> 00:30:29.765
He will keep silent about what he knows.

00:30:33.787 --> 00:30:37.545
Today, Cosco has become a role model for Calabrian mobsters.

00:30:38.748 --> 00:30:42.465
For the 'Ndrangheta, Cosco is a symbol, an example to follow.

00:30:44.512 --> 00:30:47.623
He is the beacon which lights the way that all the mafia must follow.

00:30:48.934 --> 00:30:51.373
Even if it means killing a member of your own family,

00:30:52.231 --> 00:30:53.981
honour killings purify blood.

00:30:54.670 --> 00:30:56.012
You must always keep silent.

00:30:56.731 --> 00:31:00.738
And everything you do must be in the interests of the criminal organisation.

00:31:01.213 --> 00:31:02.679
That's what the&nbsp;'Ndrangheta&nbsp;is.

00:31:03.417 --> 00:31:10.124
Today, Luigi Bonaventura is collaborating with police all over Europe, trying to dismantle the&nbsp;'Ndrangheta.

00:31:12.003 --> 00:31:18.496
For the most discreet mafia organizations have, over the last century, become a huge criminal multinational.

00:31:19.355 --> 00:31:25.527
Its main source of revenue is cocaine, and its estimated turnover is 53 billion euros.

00:31:27.579 --> 00:31:31.897
In Calabria, one man knows better than anyone the power of the&nbsp;'Ndrangheta.

00:31:33.160 --> 00:31:38.212
Barricaded in his courthouse, he has fought a relentless battle with it for 26 years.

00:31:38.582 --> 00:31:41.961
Nicola Gratteri is deputy prosecutor in Reggio Calabria.

00:31:43.461 --> 00:31:49.469
The&nbsp;'Ndrangheta&nbsp;has always been thought of as a poor mafia organisation, a category B mafia, which wasn't worth worrying about.

00:31:49.922 --> 00:31:51.798
But in fact, they were being underestimated.

00:31:51.848 --> 00:31:53.897
The 'Ndrangheta has done a lot of business.

00:31:56.932 --> 00:32:00.355
Every month, the&nbsp;'Ndrangheta&nbsp;brings tons of cocaine into Europe.

00:32:01.496 --> 00:32:03.961
And most of it shipped by boat from South America.

00:32:05.582 --> 00:32:07.179
Its main ports are Hamburg, Rotterdam,

00:32:08.624 --> 00:32:10.198
Antwerp, Barcelona,

00:32:10.794 --> 00:32:14.171
and, most importantly, of course, Gioia Tauro in Calabria.

00:32:15.811 --> 00:32:19.390
Here in 2002, 2 tons of cocaine were seized.

00:32:20.327 --> 00:32:24.983
It had been hidden in jars of vegetables, tins, furniture, and even blocks of cement.

00:32:28.220 --> 00:32:32.212
Today, the&nbsp;'Ndrangheta&nbsp;has an almost complete monopoly over the importing of cocaine into Europe.

00:32:32.321 --> 00:32:36.368
It has men in Colombia, in other parts of South America.

00:32:38.124 --> 00:32:40.624
Their job is to buy the cocaine at the lowest price.

00:32:43.201 --> 00:32:53.561
The cocaine was transported in these 31 suitcases, registered to names of fictitious passengers on the same commercial flight, originating in Caracas, Venezuela and heading for Roissy.

00:32:54.326 --> 00:32:56.765
Sometimes, drugs also arrive by plane.

00:32:57.352 --> 00:33:00.816
As they did here at this airport in Paris last September.

00:33:02.291 --> 00:33:10.705
The biggest cocaine haul in France, 1.3 tonnes of pure drugs held by the Criminal Investigation Department, worth 50 million euros.

00:33:12.608 --> 00:33:19.476
Important takings, but only representative of 10% of the drugs imported by the&nbsp;'Ndrangheta&nbsp;in Europe.

00:33:20.436 --> 00:33:24.615
Once the cocaine arrives on the continent, a vast network gets to work.

00:33:25.443 --> 00:33:25.757
Europe...

00:33:28.000 --> 00:33:30.243
is full of Calabrian mafia on the run.

00:33:31.880 --> 00:33:32.861
While they're at large,

00:33:34.541 --> 00:33:35.502
they sell cocaine.

00:33:38.905 --> 00:33:42.108
An effective web, discreet, highly elusive.

00:33:43.351 --> 00:33:46.897
For the police, the fight against the&nbsp;'Ndrangheta&nbsp;is particularly difficult.

00:33:48.374 --> 00:33:57.627
Unlike other mafia organisations, which have a pyramid-like structure, the&nbsp;'Ndrangheta&nbsp;is formed of hundreds of families that are autonomous, independent one from another.

00:33:58.725 --> 00:34:04.300
Sometimes these families kill amongst themselves, as they did in Duisburg in Germany.

00:34:05.078 --> 00:34:10.184
It was in 2007 that two clans waged war for the first time outside of Italy.

00:34:12.847 --> 00:34:19.975
Settling of accounts, Calabrian style. In Germany, 6 Italian immigrants were found dead, killed by several bullets, including one in the head, in Duisburg.

00:34:20.142 --> 00:34:23.892
The victims, aged between 16 and 39, were all linked to the Calabrian mafia.

00:34:25.456 --> 00:34:30.155
In one of the victims' pockets was the image of the archangel Michael, with his head burnt.

00:34:30.795 --> 00:34:31.554
A signature.

00:34:32.675 --> 00:34:37.199
The world discovers the&nbsp;'Ndrangheta, and the police intensify their surveillance.

00:34:43.550 --> 00:34:53.874
In Calabria, 2 years later, during the famous pilgrimage of Our Lady of Polsi, thanks to CCTV, the authorities identify the most powerful&nbsp;'Ndrangheta&nbsp;bosses.

00:34:55.472 --> 00:34:56.239
The Big Boss.

00:34:56.887 --> 00:35:00.412
This old man is Domenico&nbsp;Oppedisano, aged 80.

00:35:02.054 --> 00:35:04.809
He's holding an informal meeting outside the church.

00:35:09.740 --> 00:35:12.767
What we've managed to do would never have been possible without me.

00:35:13.179 --> 00:35:13.747
We know.

00:35:16.229 --> 00:35:20.958
Thanks to this video, the police discovered the existence of a secret body, Crimine.

00:35:22.574 --> 00:35:27.711
At the heart of the Calabrian mafia, they check that rules and codes are respected among the Cosco.

00:35:28.731 --> 00:35:33.153
The Crimine belongs to no one, but makes decisions for everyone. They have to represent us.

00:35:34.559 --> 00:35:37.278
After this recording, inquiries were launched.

00:35:38.746 --> 00:35:44.208
Nearly 50 mobsters were arrested, including the Big Boss, Domenico Oppedisano.

00:35:44.887 --> 00:35:46.630
Today, he spends his time in prison.

00:35:49.505 --> 00:35:52.943
Since then, the fight against the&nbsp;'Ndrangheta&nbsp;has doubled in intensity.

00:35:54.288 --> 00:35:56.088
The police have toppled other clans.

00:35:57.170 --> 00:36:04.079
Notably, in April 2010, that of the Pesce family, one of the most powerful on the Gioia Tauro plain.

00:36:06.282 --> 00:36:09.181
40 mobsters from the clan are arrested and imprisoned.

00:36:10.086 --> 00:36:15.086
Among them Giuseppina Pesce, known as Giusy, the Big Boss's niece.

00:36:15.920 --> 00:36:20.056
Aged 32, and a mother of 2 children, Giusy can't cope with prison.

00:36:21.816 --> 00:36:26.931
After two suicide attempts, she decides to collaborate with the law and denounce her clan.

00:36:31.850 --> 00:36:36.666
Alessandra Cerreti is the prosecutor who persuaded Giusy to betray her family.

00:36:42.353 --> 00:36:48.247
First, she made a flowchart of the clan with the role of each member of her family.

00:36:48.537 --> 00:36:52.417
She showed all the criminal activities undertaken by the clan.

00:36:53.003 --> 00:36:56.148
She listed their assets, one by one.

00:36:57.387 --> 00:36:59.809
Everything the clan uses for money laundering.

00:37:01.556 --> 00:37:04.617
Giusy's evidence has terrible repercussions for her family.

00:37:06.634 --> 00:37:09.697
Francesco Pesce, her cousin, the boss of the clan, is arrested.

00:37:11.539 --> 00:37:18.306
He is found in his secret hideout, built almost unbelievably, under a criminal investigation yard.

00:37:20.478 --> 00:37:24.159
Bunkers like this, the Pesce family has eight of them in the area.

00:37:25.300 --> 00:37:27.174
They were all found thanks to Giusy.

00:37:32.521 --> 00:37:34.572
We were able to visit one of the hideouts.

00:37:35.380 --> 00:37:36.541
Built under a stable.

00:37:40.196 --> 00:37:44.001
Two rooms, a kitchen, a bathroom, air conditioning,

00:37:47.340 --> 00:37:48.855
television, internet,

00:37:49.432 --> 00:37:51.134
and, not forgetting, the prayer corner.

00:37:52.073 --> 00:37:54.156
Enough to keep you going for several months.

00:37:55.276 --> 00:38:01.991
Again, thanks to Giusy, the police seized assets from her family that had a value of 220 million euros.

00:38:03.558 --> 00:38:08.747
Including the ultimate symbol of their power, this huge villa overlooking the town of Rosarno.

00:38:09.916 --> 00:38:12.489
It is extremely golden and kitsch in the extreme.

00:38:15.614 --> 00:38:18.097
The Calabrian version of Scarface's mansion.

00:38:21.360 --> 00:38:25.808
The 25h of September, 2000, the court in Palmi, in the south of Calabria.

00:38:26.570 --> 00:38:29.145
Unusually, the Italian court has allowed us to film.

00:38:30.240 --> 00:38:39.248
Here present is Mrs. Giuseppina Pesce, born in Gioia Tauro on the 24th of September, 1979.

00:38:41.327 --> 00:38:45.364
Today, Giusy Pesce must once more give evidence against her clan.

00:38:46.273 --> 00:38:48.893
For security reasons, she is not present in the court.

00:38:49.483 --> 00:38:52.077
The interrogation takes place by videoconference.

00:38:52.795 --> 00:38:57.248
Giusy is the small, dark head with her back to us, opposite a clerk of the court.

00:38:58.577 --> 00:39:04.138
The Pesce family is the one which has total control over the town of Rosarno.

00:39:05.543 --> 00:39:08.374
They know everything that happens in Rosarno.

00:39:09.884 --> 00:39:11.063
If a shop opens,

00:39:11.867 --> 00:39:14.047
it must be acceptable to the clan.

00:39:15.806 --> 00:39:25.570
If there's an argument, a murder, anything that happens must be run past the boss of the Pesce clan, by my family.

00:39:26.992 --> 00:39:29.643
Every time she talks, Giusy goes further.

00:39:30.199 --> 00:39:32.256
And gives more explicit information.

00:39:35.057 --> 00:39:41.802
My brother collaborated with the Pelle family for drug trafficking and raids.

00:39:43.092 --> 00:39:45.129
He worked with Gaetano Pelle.

00:39:46.069 --> 00:39:48.130
With him, it was gun running.

00:39:48.880 --> 00:39:53.904
They spoke about pistols, machine guns, rifles.

00:39:57.130 --> 00:39:58.994
Giusy now lives with her children.

00:39:59.447 --> 00:40:01.469
Hidden and protected by state officials.

00:40:02.570 --> 00:40:04.995
And they are the only ones with the right to talk to her.

00:40:08.137 --> 00:40:12.811
We spent 6 months negotiating with the Italian authorities in the hope of interviewing her.

00:40:14.722 --> 00:40:20.545
It was worth it in the end, as we get what is to this day the only interview she has ever given.

00:40:21.364 --> 00:40:23.379
We have a meeting in a military barracks.

00:40:24.106 --> 00:40:26.912
Giusy is already there, tapping her mobile phone.

00:40:28.779 --> 00:40:31.929
She leaves it to her lawyer to establish conditions for the interview.

00:40:35.101 --> 00:40:38.990
Don't ask very personal questions, nothing too personal or precise.

00:40:41.420 --> 00:40:44.197
We will give more details later when her trial is over.

00:40:48.375 --> 00:40:51.054
Giusy is still on trial for her mafia connections.

00:40:52.415 --> 00:40:54.328
Is that OK for you, Giusy?

00:40:55.608 --> 00:40:59.694
Don't worry, I'll ask you questions, but if you don't feel comfortable, don't answer.

00:41:01.409 --> 00:41:02.684
The interview can begin.

00:41:03.547 --> 00:41:05.728
Giusy doesn't want to be seen as a heroine.

00:41:08.367 --> 00:41:11.075
I am the daughter of Salvatore Pesce.

00:41:12.169 --> 00:41:15.072
I belong to the mafia family of Rosarno.

00:41:17.492 --> 00:41:20.710
Until 2010, I lived in Rosarno.

00:41:22.820 --> 00:41:24.007
I led a normal life.

00:41:24.619 --> 00:41:28.766
I was married, I had 3 children, I had a job.

00:41:31.808 --> 00:41:34.556
I always worked in my father's companies.

00:41:35.666 --> 00:41:38.516
Supermarkets, clothes shops,

00:41:39.851 --> 00:41:41.916
or in my father-in-law's business.

00:41:43.625 --> 00:41:46.694
We women, our role was to help the men.

00:41:47.469 --> 00:41:49.561
To support them when they were in prison.

00:41:51.047 --> 00:41:51.827
To visit them.

00:41:53.367 --> 00:41:57.510
And if it was necessary, pass information on to the mafia outside,

00:41:58.791 --> 00:41:59.775
to the brothers,

00:42:01.298 --> 00:42:02.798
the bosses of the clans.

00:42:07.769 --> 00:42:10.237
Even if you know it's a crime.

00:42:12.971 --> 00:42:13.565
You do it.

00:42:16.761 --> 00:42:21.737
What Giusy is most proud of is managing to extricate her children from the clutches of the mafia.

00:42:23.532 --> 00:42:26.996
My son had already been conditioned, like the others.

00:42:28.657 --> 00:42:31.875
He would also have had a future in the mafia.

00:42:33.201 --> 00:42:34.622
That's how it works.

00:42:35.768 --> 00:42:38.133
At 18, they would have given him a gun.

00:42:39.170 --> 00:42:42.672
I wanted something different for him, for him to study.

00:42:43.208 --> 00:42:45.155
But no, he can't study.

00:42:45.771 --> 00:42:46.866
Why should he study?

00:42:47.568 --> 00:42:50.307
He will do what his father did, what his uncle did.

00:42:51.024 --> 00:42:56.907
I was against that, of course, but in the end, they are the ones who are in charge, not us.

00:42:58.239 --> 00:43:01.287
My children were out there, alone, without me.

00:43:02.266 --> 00:43:04.625
I would probably have been inside for years.

00:43:05.425 --> 00:43:09.219
Time would have passed, and they would still have been there.

00:43:10.692 --> 00:43:11.777
I needed to protect them.

00:43:15.559 --> 00:43:19.508
Since Giusy's arrest, a large number of the Pesce family are in prison.

00:43:23.061 --> 00:43:26.695
On this security camera is Rocco Pesce, one of her uncles.

00:43:27.827 --> 00:43:29.289
Three women have come to talk to him.

00:43:30.311 --> 00:43:34.822
He affirms that he is still in control of the town and issues a death threat against Giusy.

00:43:37.577 --> 00:43:39.240
You think I don't know what's going on?

00:43:39.678 --> 00:43:40.615
I know everything.

00:43:40.854 --> 00:43:43.245
I have spies everywhere who write to me.

00:43:43.855 --> 00:43:46.224
They tell me everything. They're my people.

00:43:47.054 --> 00:43:49.115
I don't need to see, I know everything.

00:43:49.788 --> 00:43:51.507
We're losing all form of dignity.

00:43:54.411 --> 00:43:59.735
The bitch that no longer looks you in the eye must be killed quickly, or else she'll scratch you all over.

00:44:06.438 --> 00:44:07.634
We went to Rosarno.

00:44:11.324 --> 00:44:16.613
It has a population of 12,000, and the highest number of crimes linked to the&nbsp;'Ndrangheta.

00:44:19.058 --> 00:44:20.820
Giusy's grandmother still lives here.

00:44:23.344 --> 00:44:27.436
She has always had a fruit and vegetable stall, despite the wealth of her clan.

00:44:27.829 --> 00:44:28.548
We approach her.

00:44:31.147 --> 00:44:32.150
Good morning, madam.

00:44:33.150 --> 00:44:34.770
Are you Giusy's grandmother?

00:44:35.867 --> 00:44:38.095
Yes, but she's not here.

00:44:38.608 --> 00:44:39.853
What do you think she did?

00:44:42.056 --> 00:44:43.744
She's a naive, young girl.

00:44:44.270 --> 00:44:45.541
She understands.

00:44:46.137 --> 00:44:46.885
She'd had it.

00:44:47.482 --> 00:44:49.439
And you know what the judges did?

00:44:49.947 --> 00:44:52.853
They tricked her into saying things that are not true.

00:44:53.534 --> 00:44:56.003
Everything she said is false.

00:44:57.215 --> 00:44:59.519
All my children are in prison.

00:45:00.181 --> 00:45:03.748
I'm just a little old lady on my own.

00:45:04.053 --> 00:45:06.951
And if I fall, there's no one left to look after me.

00:45:07.254 --> 00:45:08.365
I'm right, no?

00:45:08.488 --> 00:45:13.257
Soon I will die, and I will die alone, with my sorrow, with no one.

00:45:13.962 --> 00:45:17.054
But if they're all in prison, they must have done something.

00:45:18.156 --> 00:45:19.001
Nothing.

00:45:19.278 --> 00:45:20.070
I swear.

00:45:20.572 --> 00:45:22.115
My son died in prison.

00:45:22.444 --> 00:45:24.287
They didn't give him his medication.

00:45:24.494 --> 00:45:25.995
He died in prison.

00:45:26.072 --> 00:45:28.115
It's a sin against God.

00:45:28.165 --> 00:45:29.781
He has four children.

00:45:30.093 --> 00:45:32.006
Why didn't they take him to hospital?

00:45:32.122 --> 00:45:37.776
Because his name is Pesce. So? Just because your name is Pesce doesn't mean you have done something wrong.

00:45:38.333 --> 00:45:40.130
My children haven't killed anyone.

00:45:40.771 --> 00:45:44.427
They haven't stolen. They haven't set a bad example to young people.

00:45:44.771 --> 00:45:47.114
I know that they want to kill Giusy for what she did.

00:45:48.279 --> 00:45:49.935
Who wants to kill her?

00:45:49.985 --> 00:45:52.151
She's been gone for such a long time.

00:45:52.376 --> 00:45:53.969
Who could want to kill her?

00:45:55.407 --> 00:45:57.709
We don't have permission to talk to Mrs. Pesce.

00:45:59.584 --> 00:46:03.231
In less than 5 minutes, a member of the clan comes to ask us to leave.

00:46:03.755 --> 00:46:04.972
Please turn off that camera.

00:46:05.277 --> 00:46:06.947
Of course. Stop the camera.

00:46:07.122 --> 00:46:09.320
We don't want any trouble. There's enough here already.

00:46:14.316 --> 00:46:16.692
Giusy has caught trouble at the heart of the town.

00:46:18.995 --> 00:46:22.068
Few women in the Calabrian mafia are prepared to forgive her.

00:46:26.390 --> 00:46:29.821
If you knew where Giusy was, would you tell the&nbsp;'Ndrangheta?

00:46:31.702 --> 00:46:32.023
Yes.

00:46:33.402 --> 00:46:35.197
Because she didn't honour the code.

00:46:36.425 --> 00:46:38.309
She sent the mafia to prison.

00:46:38.824 --> 00:46:40.760
She denounced them.

00:46:41.049 --> 00:46:45.097
&nbsp;So, yes, I would tell them where she is, so they could kill her.

00:46:46.735 --> 00:46:50.503
She has betrayed her own kind and she should be punished.

00:46:51.081 --> 00:46:56.034
Giusy is a dead woman walking for the 'Ndrangheta, forever.

00:46:56.523 --> 00:46:57.985
No one will forget her.

00:46:58.425 --> 00:46:59.407
That's not possible.

00:47:01.809 --> 00:47:04.793
Despite the risks, another young woman rebelled.

00:47:06.361 --> 00:47:10.473
Maria Concetta Cacciola decided to follow Giusy's example.

00:47:11.270 --> 00:47:16.505
Aged 31, mother of three children, she was married at the age of 14 to a mobster.

00:47:17.489 --> 00:47:19.786
She, too, denounced her clan to the authorities.

00:47:21.083 --> 00:47:25.507
She told us, I want to do the same as Giusy, to tell you everything.

00:47:26.606 --> 00:47:27.467
She asked for help,

00:47:28.276 --> 00:47:31.653
wanted to be placed under protection, which we did immediately.

00:47:32.594 --> 00:47:33.273
We moved her.

00:47:35.273 --> 00:47:38.083
But after a while she missed her family too much,

00:47:39.492 --> 00:47:40.839
and she made the mistake of

00:47:41.932 --> 00:47:43.100
contacting them.

00:47:44.444 --> 00:47:46.559
A fatal mistake for Maria Concetta.

00:47:47.710 --> 00:47:49.257
Her mother begged her to come home.

00:47:49.757 --> 00:47:50.492
It was a trap.

00:47:52.092 --> 00:47:55.335
The police recorded the last telephone conversation between the two women.

00:47:56.501 --> 00:47:57.027
Hello.

00:47:58.229 --> 00:47:58.784
Mama.

00:48:00.485 --> 00:48:03.786
Papa said you didn't want to come home because you were ashamed.

00:48:05.722 --> 00:48:12.182
Clever blackmail by a mother to get her daughter to come home in order to punish her and save the honour of the clan.

00:48:13.527 --> 00:48:14.309
I'm finished.

00:48:14.809 --> 00:48:15.734
I'm dying.

00:48:16.074 --> 00:48:17.231
Do you understand?

00:48:17.684 --> 00:48:19.512
I understand, but leave me alone.

00:48:19.965 --> 00:48:21.387
No, you don't understand.

00:48:22.108 --> 00:48:23.109
They are using you.

00:48:23.472 --> 00:48:24.577
They've turned your head.

00:48:25.438 --> 00:48:27.845
Now you must decide between them and us.

00:48:29.059 --> 00:48:37.278
If you love your children, if you love us, your brothers, your father and me, like we love you, you must come home.

00:48:37.864 --> 00:48:38.443
It's simple.

00:48:39.443 --> 00:48:41.021
Maria Concetta obeys her mother.

00:48:41.661 --> 00:48:43.083
Her return home will be brief.

00:48:45.059 --> 00:48:49.356
The next day, her parents will claim that she has committed suicide by drinking acid.

00:48:51.371 --> 00:48:56.567
Acid is often used by the 'Ndrangheta as it has great symbolic value.

00:48:59.007 --> 00:49:01.349
It's mainly used to clean toilets.

00:49:03.550 --> 00:49:08.311
And it enters into the mouth, the same mouth which was open to talk.

00:49:09.413 --> 00:49:12.788
And so it sends a strong message to the outside world.

00:49:13.233 --> 00:49:15.498
"Look, what happens to those who talk.

00:49:16.155 --> 00:49:20.092
Like the filth in toilets, it destroys both inside and out."

00:49:22.452 --> 00:49:23.814
I was devastated

00:49:24.670 --> 00:49:26.218
because I knew Cetta.

00:49:26.733 --> 00:49:27.639
We were friends.

00:49:29.853 --> 00:49:33.074
It was obvious that if she went home, they were going to kill her.

00:49:35.317 --> 00:49:37.581
A woman who rebels causes fear.

00:49:38.442 --> 00:49:39.659
Why do women rebel?

00:49:40.567 --> 00:49:41.942
Why has this one rebelled?

00:49:44.003 --> 00:49:45.606
If one has, then others might,

00:49:46.293 --> 00:49:47.824
and then they will lose control.

00:49:48.574 --> 00:49:48.856
Why?

00:49:49.871 --> 00:49:52.356
Is it a disgrace if they can't look after their wives?

00:49:55.324 --> 00:49:55.824
Yes.

00:49:59.016 --> 00:50:00.410
They lose credibility.

00:50:01.697 --> 00:50:03.630
A man who can't manage his wife?

00:50:04.898 --> 00:50:08.297
If he can't control her, like my case, it's serious.

00:50:13.797 --> 00:50:17.498
For the moment, only three women have rebelled in the Calabrian mafia.

00:50:18.719 --> 00:50:20.077
Two have paid with their lives.

00:50:21.766 --> 00:50:24.516
The others remain silent, and carry out their duty.

00:50:26.811 --> 00:50:29.322
To give their sons the strength to kill.

00:50:33.056 --> 00:50:35.678
Mothers sing to their children, even in the cradle.

00:50:37.945 --> 00:50:44.038
Look at my son how handsome he is,

00:50:45.505 --> 00:50:51.080
how he resembles his daddy.

00:50:52.461 --> 00:50:58.305
And you, you must hurry to grow up,

00:50:59.734 --> 00:51:05.196
to learn to handle weapons and knives.

00:51:06.447 --> 00:51:09.546
A culture of crime omnipresent in Calabria.

00:51:10.431 --> 00:51:12.400
Even Giusy remains pessimistic.

00:51:13.650 --> 00:51:17.861
Seen from the outside, you might think that they have been stopped.

00:51:20.196 --> 00:51:27.019
That they are less powerful, but the 'Ndrangheta is powerful and it is everywhere.

00:51:29.032 --> 00:51:33.307
There is always someone to take over, there's always someone.

00:51:39.809 --> 00:51:43.614
My son, you must avenge your father.

00:51:43.664 --> 00:51:46.550
Go to sleep, baby, go to sleep.

